  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x70D3" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 2 - Ignition Timing Surface - High-Detonation State</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x1D300; 16 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. High-detonation hot timing-state surface. It supplies active sample ffff160f only when ffff2466.bit6 is set; the reference remains high-octane surface 0x9A1A. Coordinator 000493e8 also looks it up independently for the conditional signed Q8 difference from 0x9A1A. Common-definition Map 2 storage is projected from 0x97CA. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. This view edits mask 0x7F and preserves the other bits in each cell. Knock evaluation 0004a238 and coordinator 000493e8 form the state loop that updates the selector for a later pass. A code-proven correction path exists through ffff22fa; code does not prove this surface as a direct final angle. The physical name and scale match homolog EV18A 0x9b76. Definition address projected from JK08A 00009b1a through JK08A-JK78C.definition-addresses.csv: unique same-contract accessor preserves the second 16x16 ignition surface and operand order.</description>
