  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x3B71" flags="0x0">
    <title>Map 4 - DFCO Low-Speed Intermediate Restore RPM Threshold</title>
    <description>Exact JK78C. Address 0x1E9E0; 1 rows x 16 columns; uint8; map confidence candidate. Coolant-indexed low-speed upper/intermediate-restore RPM threshold in FUN 00050018. At speed count below 4, RPM above lower table 00012818 and at or below this adjusted threshold returns class 2; RPM strictly above it returns class 0. Common-definition Map 4 storage is projected from 0x13E72. Stock firmware does not reference this allocated storage; it becomes runtime-active only with the project map-switching patch. The adjusted result is stored in ffff1778 after the same coolant floors and runtime offsets as the lower table. The table is always interpolated, but every speed-count-4-or-above branch reachable with stock ROM8[00008b3f].bit7=0 and ROM8[0000870c].bit7=0 ignores it. It remains a live stock calibration for the low-speed class-2 band rather than a moving DFCO veto. The moving target-vehicle capture cannot validate this table because its selected samples are all above the stock speed boundary. Result disposition: inline_comparison. Definition address projected from JK08A 0001298c through JK08A-JK78C.definition-addresses.csv: unique accessor and coordinator preserve lookup role and order. Static diagnostic context: Engine Coolant Temperature [code, homologous_community, via map evidence: indexed_by].</description>
